# cut-v0 — animatic

Built from director `direction/script.md` + `direction/shot-list.md` at director 587111f400ddcc15509533592d99ca62beaed7ea
with `tools/animatic.py` (EDL `edl.json`, scratch subtitles `scratch.srt`) and rendered with `tools/conform.py`.
Picture: one slate per shot (framing, palette, what must be seen); end title is final. Sound: none (silent AAC track) — the scratch subtitles stand in for the read.

**Timing method.** Each line is laid at the narrator pace the script asks for (160 wpm, +0.2 s), starting at its target time or 0.35 s after the previous line ends, whichever is later; each shot moves with its first line. At that pace lines 3, 16–17 and 20–23 overrun their slots, so the cut runs **123.67 s** (window 115–125). The real read replaces this estimate: once sound-designer publishes the line WAVs, cut-v1 is timed to them.

